---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Launch a debugging session

Identify the target run with exactly one of --run-id (preferred) or
--session-id.

Example:
  snouty debug \
    --run-id 9043254f65c9c65d63fe043a0abfc7fc-53-1 \
    --input-hash 6057726200491963783 \
    --vtime 329.8037810830865 \
    --title "stalled leader election" \
    --description "debug this moment" \
    --recipients "team@example.com"

Extra parameters can be passed with --param, as for `snouty launch`. A --param
cannot replace the value of a dedicated flag, such as --title:
  snouty debug --run-id <run_id> --input-hash <hash> --vtime <vtime> \
    --param attrs.team=payments

The response holds the new session's run ID in `runId`. The session starts at
the moment that it debugs. Wait until it is ready, then run commands at that
moment:
  snouty runs wait <session_run_id> --until ready
  snouty runs exec <session_run_id> <hash> <vtime> 'ps aux'

Add --json for machine-readable output. The response prints as one JSON object:
  snouty debug --json --run-id <run_id> --input-hash <hash> --vtime <vtime> |
    jq -r .runId

Usage: snouty debug [OPTIONS] --input-hash <INPUT_HASH> --vtime <VTIME> <--run-id <RUN_ID>|--session-id <SESSION_ID>>

Options:
      --run-id <RUN_ID>
          Run ID of the test run to debug (preferred; give it or the session ID,
          not both)

      --session-id <SESSION_ID>
          Session ID of the test run to debug (give it or the run ID, not both)

      --input-hash <INPUT_HASH>
          Input hash identifying the moment to debug

      --vtime <VTIME>
          Virtual time identifying the moment to debug

      --title <TITLE>
          Debugging session title, shown as the test name in the run list

      --description <DESCRIPTION>
          Debugging session description

      --recipients <RECIPIENTS>
          Report recipients (semicolon-delimited email addresses)

      --param <PARAMS>
          Extra parameters as key=value pairs (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
